                <pb facs="0917" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg797"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September 22,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee instructs Mr. Meyer to inform the Russian Government that the Japanese
                    Government intends to carry out the arrangement for the exchange of prisoners
                    soon after the ratification of the treaty by the respective sovereigns, and that
                    in this respect the treaty will operate even before the exchange of the
                    ratifications.)</p>
            </div>
